WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.183 --> 00:00:02.556
♪ I've been living with
drama, I'm on my knees ♪

00:00:02.556 --> 00:00:04.180
♪ Can you pray for me, Mama ♪

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:06.670
- I've been kicking people
off the Apollo stage,

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:08.070
for what, 31 years?

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:10.595
If you're not good enough,
you get booed off the stage.

00:00:10.595 --> 00:00:12.145
(laughs)
The audience love it.

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:17.710
♪ So good, so good, not so good ♪

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:19.430
I'm C.P. Lacey, the executioner

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:21.420
at the world famous Apollo Theater.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.960
All together now, “Boo!”

00:00:27.523 --> 00:00:29.773
(laughing)

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:35.467
Welcome to the Apollo
Amateur Night, are you ready?

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:42.990
Amateur Night at the Apollo
is the granddaddy to all

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:44.890
of these shows that you look at today:

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:48.470
“X-Factor,” “America's Got
Talent,” “American Idol.”

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:51.710
You come and you sing or you
dance or you do your magic

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:55.180
or tell a joke or poem, and
the audience will decide

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:57.290
whether you go on to the next level

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:01.980
or whether you get booed off of the stage.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:03.687
That's where I come in, grrrr!

00:01:04.765 --> 00:01:07.348
(upbeat music)

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:11.450
My role is to educate
you about your own talent

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:13.100
or lack thereof.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:15.590
Our booing policy is this:

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:19.140
There is a boo here, a boo
there, a boo here, then the boos

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:20.410
just get paramount.

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:22.400
We have a noise meter back stage,

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.425
and when it reaches a certain boo level,

00:01:24.425 --> 00:01:26.523
the next thing you know there is a siren,

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:29.780
enter the executioner to kick you off

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:31.392
of my stage.

00:01:31.392 --> 00:01:34.030
(audience applauding)

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:37.770
The executioner character
changes after every execution.

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:39.560
At the top of the show,
I'll gong someone off

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:40.781
as Michael Jackson

00:01:40.781 --> 00:01:43.531
♪ You've been hit by,
you've been struck by ♪

00:01:43.531 --> 00:01:44.800
♪ A boo criminal ♪

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:46.696
- The Godfather of Soul, James Brown

00:01:46.696 --> 00:01:50.406
♪ So true, so true, you just got a boo ♪

00:01:50.406 --> 00:01:53.120
♪ Da da da da, hey, hit me ♪

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:53.953
Prince.

00:01:53.953 --> 00:01:56.796
♪ Di di di did boo ♪

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:02.680
The Apollo Theater is a place
where we, as African Americans

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:04.570
could go and perform.

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:08.410
Folks like Ella Fitzgerald,
Sammy Davis, Jr., James Brown,

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:11.283
and Lauren Hill have
graced the Apollo stage.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:15.240
I don't enjoy kicking people
off the stage, per se.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:18.340
If time allows, I try to get
to the person who got booed off

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:21.890
the stage, and just encourage
them and console them.

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:24.900
Go back to the woodshed, learn
your craft, and come back.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:28.000
And when you're very, very
good, we'll give you the claps.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.953
The Apollo always invites you
to come back and try again.

00:02:32.007 --> 00:02:33.298
(audience applauding and cheering)

00:02:33.298 --> 00:02:36.458
- Thank you, man, thank you Apollo!

00:02:36.458 --> 00:02:39.987
- Every week, without fail, when they say,

00:02:39.987 --> 00:02:42.470
"Here is the executioner
saying goodnight to you folks,

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:43.310
thanks for coming in,"

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:47.504
there's always someone that
goes, "Boo, I hate you!"

00:02:47.504 --> 00:02:48.337
(laughs)

00:02:48.337 --> 00:02:51.581
They just love being a part
of the Apollo audience.

00:02:51.581 --> 00:02:54.748
(audience applauding)

